# BMKG Weather & Temperature API — Bandung, Kecamatan Coblong

## Location code (kode wilayah)

We use **Kecamatan Coblong**, Kota Bandung, Jawa Barat:

- **Kode: 32.73.02**
  - 32 = Jawa Barat (provinsi)
  - 73 = Kota Bandung (kabupaten/kota)
  - 02 = Kecamatan Coblong

Kelurahan di Coblong (for finer-grained data): 32.73.02.1001 (Cipaganti), 32.73.02.1002 (Lebak Gede), 32.73.02.1003 (Sadang Serang), 32.73.02.1004 (Dago), 32.73.02.1005 (Sekeloa), 32.73.02.1006 (Lebak Siliwangi).

## API endpoint (prakiraan cuaca)

Public forecast API (weather & temperature for the whole city / by region):

  https://api.bmkg.go.id/publik/prakiraan-cuaca?adm4={kode_wilayah_tingkat_iv}

**For Coblong (kecamatan-level):**

  curl "https://api.bmkg.go.id/publik/prakiraan-cuaca?adm4=32.73.02"

**Example for a single kelurahan (Jakarta):**

  curl "https://api.bmkg.go.id/publik/prakiraan-cuaca?adm4=31.71.03.1001"

If the API expects a 4-part code for Coblong, try one of the kelurahan codes above (e.g. adm4=32.73.02.1001).

## BMKG web page (human-readable)

Prakiraan cuaca Kecamatan Coblong:

  https://www.bmkg.go.id/cuaca/prakiraan-cuaca/32.73.02

This page shows temperature range (°C), humidity (%), and weather (e.g. Berawan, Hujan Ringan) per period.

## Use in this project

- Weather → `cuaca` (map BMKG condition to a numeric code, e.g. 0=Cerah, 1=Berawan, 2=Hujan Ringan).
- Temperature → `suhu` (use mid of min–max or the value provided; °C).
- Kelembapan (humidity) from BMKG can feed `kelembapan` (soil moisture can be replaced or combined with sensor data later).
- Run `python fetch_bmkg_coblong.py` to fetch for 32.73.02 and append/update CSV for training.
